al hashes when comparing a trusted computed hmac sum to an untrusted input sum if an attacker can send a zeroed buffer in place of a pre-computed sum.\u00a0 It is also possible to force a derived key to be all zeros instead of an unpredictable value.\u00a0 This may have follow-on implications for the Go TLS stack.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a vulnerability was found in golang fips openssl. this flaw allows a malicious user to randomly cause an uninitialized buffer length variable with a zeroed buffer to be returned in fips mode. it may also be possible to force a false positive match between non-equal hashes when comparing a trusted computed hmac sum to an untrusted input sum if an attacker can send a zeroed buffer in place of a pre-computed sum.\u00a0 it is also possible to force a derived key to be all zeros instead of an unpredictable value.\u00a0 this may have follow-on implications for the go tls stack."},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7 Extended Lifecycle Support","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 7 extended lifecycle support"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 8"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8.4 Advanced Mission Critical Update Support","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 8.4 advanced mission critical update support"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8.4 Extended Update Support Long-Life Add-On","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 8.4 extended update support long-life add-on"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8.6 Advanced Mission Critical Update S